WEBVTT

00:02.380 --> 00:04.890
This meat's so good!

00:05.480 --> 00:06.930
It's so tender!

00:06.930 --> 00:09.860
Is the one you've got there Breakfast Set B?

00:09.860 --> 00:12.370
Nope, Set C.

00:12.700 --> 00:14.850
That one was good, too...

00:15.890 --> 00:18.530
A through E were all delicious!

00:19.230 --> 00:23.390
What do you think, Chris? 
I'm going to start over with A again.

00:23.390 --> 00:26.390
Of course, so will I.

00:27.280 --> 00:30.260
Crap! Crap! I overslept!

00:30.810 --> 00:34.450
You were supposed to wake me up, Rati!

00:34.450 --> 00:36.220
Why did you oversleep?

00:36.680 --> 00:38.750
Thanks to you, I overslept too!

00:38.750 --> 00:41.570
Have your roommate wake you up!

00:41.570 --> 00:45.540
I told them they didn't have to, 
because you were going to do it!

00:45.540 --> 00:48.420
Well, that's your problem.

00:50.140 --> 00:53.500
How much are you lot eating for breakfast?!

00:54.920 --> 00:57.180
The three of you ate all this?

00:57.180 --> 01:00.740
No, I just had this one plate.

01:00.740 --> 01:02.540
So the <i>two</i> of you ate all this?

01:02.540 --> 01:04.120
Isn't that too much food for breakfast?

01:04.120 --> 01:06.430
It's normal, isn't it, Chris?

01:06.430 --> 01:09.380
Breakfast is the most 
important meal of the day.

01:11.210 --> 01:15.090
We need the energy to get us 
through the day ahead!

01:15.320 --> 01:19.060
No, you've already eaten 
enough for three days.

01:20.510 --> 01:23.200
You were amazing yesterday!

01:23.200 --> 01:25.720
You beat those three golems by yourself!

01:26.030 --> 01:27.280
Thanks.

01:28.220 --> 01:30.390
Hey, don't push me!

01:30.390 --> 01:31.600
I'm not pushing you.

01:33.070 --> 01:35.340
I'm Rati, from the squire program.

01:35.340 --> 01:37.180
This is Pram, from the knights.

01:37.180 --> 01:38.390
Hi, I'm Pram.

01:38.950 --> 01:40.860
Nice to meet you.

01:41.280 --> 01:43.530
I'm Rafinha, from the knights.

01:43.530 --> 01:45.510
I'm Inglis, from the squires.

01:45.510 --> 01:46.790
Nice to meet you!

01:46.790 --> 01:48.830
Leone, from the knights. Hi.

01:48.830 --> 01:53.170
Whisper, whisper, whisper, whisper.

01:51.140 --> 01:53.170
I think people are staring.

01:53.170 --> 01:56.640
Oh, that's because of me...

01:56.640 --> 02:03.110
A-Ah. Well, I'm not from this country, 
so that stuff doesn't mean much to me.

02:03.110 --> 02:05.060
Where are you from?

02:05.060 --> 02:07.590
Alucard. Same as Pram.

02:07.900 --> 02:10.200
So you're exchange students.

02:10.520 --> 02:13.610
Yeah. This place is nice and warm...

02:13.610 --> 02:16.390
Rati, we have to finish eating!
Class is gonna start!

02:16.390 --> 02:18.330
Oops, sorry!

02:18.600 --> 02:20.420
Pram, let's hurry up and order!

02:20.420 --> 02:22.280
We'll go with you.

02:22.610 --> 02:23.850
Let's get extra-large portions!

02:23.850 --> 02:25.600
You're still eating?!

02:40.090 --> 02:43.050
<b><u>Reborn</u></b>

02:40.090 --> 02:43.050
<b>to Master the Blade
\h\h\h\h\hFrom Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire\h\h\h\h\h</b>

02:40.090 --> 02:43.050
<b>to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire</b>

03:56.090 --> 04:00.460
<b>Episode 6     Labyrinth of Trials</b>

03:56.370 --> 04:01.050
I'm Margoose, the practical 
instructor for you freshmen!

04:01.050 --> 04:05.880
Today we'll be doing a Flying Gear 
exercise with both the knights and squires.

04:06.110 --> 04:07.980
I want to start by making one thing clear:

04:07.980 --> 04:12.300
Our war isn't just against 
the magicite beasts!

04:12.580 --> 04:13.790
We war against ourselves,

04:13.790 --> 04:17.260
pushing ourselves to the limit 
to bring peace and safety to the people!

04:17.520 --> 04:20.720
And that starts with training our bodies!

04:21.050 --> 04:24.820
So we're all going to run 
to the Flying Gear dock!

04:25.960 --> 04:29.700
And the Flying Gears are already 
out of the equation.

04:29.700 --> 04:32.710
Get moving! Double time!

04:32.710 --> 04:34.670
He's fast! I'm already losing sight of him!

04:35.350 --> 04:37.630
Where's the Flying Gear dock?

04:37.630 --> 04:41.020
I saw it yesterday. It's pretty far.

04:41.020 --> 04:43.140
We need to keep up with him!

04:43.140 --> 04:45.080
This is a nice change of pace.

04:45.790 --> 04:48.850
But just running there normally 
wouldn't be any fun at all.

04:48.850 --> 04:52.320
<i>I'll try that gravity effect that 
Principal Miliera used yesterday.</i>

04:53.190 --> 04:55.260
<i>First, I convert my aether to mana...</i>

04:55.790 --> 04:58.220
<i>And then, the way she set up her mana was...</i>

05:00.270 --> 05:03.030
<i>Okay, that'll do for now.</i>

05:04.220 --> 05:07.200
<i>If I get better, 
I bet I can make it heavier!</i>

05:08.580 --> 05:09.990
Seriously? How is she so fast?

05:10.460 --> 05:14.080
Inglis was still standing there 
when we left...

05:14.500 --> 05:16.790
Don't worry. Chris is...

05:18.100 --> 05:19.500
See?

05:21.630 --> 05:23.800
Leone, lets pick up the pace.

05:23.800 --> 05:24.910
Huh? Okay!

05:30.840 --> 05:34.800
Rati, wait! Jeez!

05:36.340 --> 05:38.270
Don't hurt yourselves trying to keep up!

05:38.270 --> 05:43.260
You're not expected to match 
my speed from the start...

05:44.960 --> 05:46.950
Can I go on ahead?

05:46.950 --> 05:48.330
S-Sure.

05:48.330 --> 05:49.520
What's your name?

05:49.520 --> 05:51.090
Inglis Eucus.

05:51.090 --> 05:53.320
You've got potential!

05:53.320 --> 05:54.750
Very good!

05:54.750 --> 05:57.790
Wait up!

05:57.790 --> 05:59.340
Wow! Not bad!

05:59.340 --> 06:04.830
Damn it! You're not even breaking 
a sweat, and I'm dying here!

06:06.190 --> 06:09.560
Looks like this year's 
freshmen have potential!

06:09.560 --> 06:10.880
Good, good.

06:10.880 --> 06:12.420
Don't forget me.

06:15.080 --> 06:17.500
W-We managed to catch up...

06:17.500 --> 06:21.370
I don't think Chris is using 
her full strength yet.

06:23.470 --> 06:27.820
I'm not gonna lose, even if it kills me!

06:28.390 --> 06:30.290
<i>That's the spirit!</i>

06:30.740 --> 06:32.010
I'll be going on ahead!

06:32.960 --> 06:34.350
How is she doing that?

06:34.750 --> 06:37.710
I told you. She wasn't 
using her full strength.

06:38.210 --> 06:43.170
If I tried to catch up to her, 
I might actually die.

06:49.100 --> 06:50.890
Wow!

06:50.890 --> 06:54.740
It's kind of exciting to look at, 
isn't it, Chris?

06:54.740 --> 06:56.050
It sure is, Rani.

06:56.740 --> 07:00.530
This is the Royal Academy. 
It's got the latest technology.

07:02.730 --> 07:06.890
Now, form up into groups. 
Two or three to a Flying Gear.

07:07.500 --> 07:09.240
Once it's outside, get on board!

07:09.240 --> 07:10.870
One of you takes the controls.

07:11.170 --> 07:14.320
The others, hang on tight 
and make sure you don't fall off!

07:14.870 --> 07:16.820
Can I go first?

07:16.820 --> 07:18.180
Sure!

07:18.180 --> 07:21.910
Squires spend a lot of time 
piloting Flying Gears, after all.

07:22.230 --> 07:24.380
Good luck, Inglis!

07:30.060 --> 07:33.260
The instructions for flying it 
are on the panel in front of you.

07:33.720 --> 07:37.010
After you activate the engine, 
switch it to flight mode.

07:38.890 --> 07:43.610
When the wings on both sides deploy, 
slowly bring up the accelerator.

07:48.520 --> 07:51.730
Wow, we're flying!

07:51.980 --> 07:54.050
Keep it up, Chris!

07:54.050 --> 07:55.210
Yeah...

07:55.210 --> 07:56.410
This is gonna work!

07:59.660 --> 08:00.960
This feels so good!

08:00.960 --> 08:02.880
And the scenery's beautiful!

08:04.090 --> 08:06.480
Aren't we going a little too fast?

08:06.480 --> 08:08.280
I'm kind of scared...

08:08.630 --> 08:11.630
But we're going to use these 
to fight the magicite beasts, right?

08:11.630 --> 08:12.920
Better get used to it.

08:12.920 --> 08:14.070
That's right!

08:14.070 --> 08:15.940
And this is the best way!

08:18.250 --> 08:20.010
Wow, Rati!

08:20.010 --> 08:21.230
You're really good at this!

08:24.240 --> 08:27.640
Looks like when it comes 
to Flying Gears, I win!

08:28.070 --> 08:29.680
I'll catch up to him.

08:34.610 --> 08:36.410
What are you doing?

08:36.810 --> 08:39.370
I hate to lose.

08:39.370 --> 08:42.130
L-Looks like... freshmen... potential!

08:42.130 --> 08:43.660
Good...

08:45.680 --> 08:48.830
Wow, she's amazing.

08:49.240 --> 08:52.040
Not only is she pretty, 
the things she does are incredible.

08:52.040 --> 08:56.670
Why are you talking like that 
when you've already got me, Rati?

08:56.670 --> 08:57.350
Like what?

08:57.350 --> 09:04.260
You never call me pretty! It's not fair!

09:00.970 --> 09:04.260
Stop it! That's dangerous!

09:23.930 --> 09:27.210
I'm sure you're tired after your classes,

09:27.210 --> 09:31.680
but we've got a special test for you today.

09:31.680 --> 09:35.160
If I call your name, step forward.

09:32.740 --> 09:34.770
A special test....

09:35.390 --> 09:40.100
Rafinha. Liselotte. Leone. Pram.

09:40.100 --> 09:41.090
Yes, ma'am!

09:44.250 --> 09:45.560
Y-Yes, ma'am!

09:45.840 --> 09:49.580
You four are the students that have been 
recommended from the knight program.

09:49.580 --> 09:51.520
And also Inglis...

09:51.520 --> 09:52.500
Yes, ma'am.

09:54.180 --> 09:57.190
You've been recommended 
from the squire program.

09:57.870 --> 10:01.200
Hey, is that the test that 
everyone was talking about?

10:01.200 --> 10:04.980
Yes! It's a huge honor just 
to be recommended for it,

10:04.980 --> 10:08.290
since it means the academy 
thinks you've got potential!

10:09.600 --> 10:12.300
The test is simple.

10:12.300 --> 10:16.100
I'm going to send you somewhere.

10:16.740 --> 10:20.180
Come back here before the time limit is up.

10:20.180 --> 10:23.300
If you can do that, you pass!

10:23.670 --> 10:25.470
Where is "somewhere"?

10:25.470 --> 10:28.280
A special space created by an Artifact!

10:28.520 --> 10:33.030
We call it the Labyrinth of Trials.

10:33.030 --> 10:38.480
It will test not only your strength, 
but your mental fortitude as well.

10:38.480 --> 10:40.200
Mental fortitude...

10:40.200 --> 10:44.200
You might find yourself suffering...

10:44.610 --> 10:49.030
But the goal is to enhance 
your mental strength as knights.

10:49.030 --> 10:50.190
Understood?

10:50.190 --> 10:50.910
Yes, ma'am!

10:52.310 --> 10:53.540
You okay?

10:54.800 --> 10:58.100
I won't let you beat me!

10:59.140 --> 11:03.180
<i>She appears to view me as a rival 
for some reason, but...</i>

11:05.170 --> 11:06.560
<i>No matter.</i>

11:11.090 --> 11:13.470
Pick a door.

11:13.790 --> 11:18.790
Each of you will find an 
appropriate trial beyond it.

11:19.560 --> 11:21.360
Now, let the test begin!

11:22.450 --> 11:24.930
Rani, Leone, be careful!

11:24.930 --> 11:26.010
You too, Chris!

11:26.010 --> 11:27.120
Let's do our best!

11:27.120 --> 11:29.370
I know I can do this!

12:07.320 --> 12:11.150
<i>This is... every foe I've ever fought!</i>

12:11.670 --> 12:13.910
<i>The perfect test!</i>

12:13.910 --> 12:15.000
Here I go!

12:15.930 --> 12:17.060
What?

12:20.200 --> 12:22.640
This isn't a test...

12:24.380 --> 12:25.720
Chris...

12:25.720 --> 12:26.700
Rani?

12:36.640 --> 12:39.330
Memories from my youth?

12:41.240 --> 12:43.670
<i>I just keep going back 
through my memories...</i>

12:43.670 --> 12:45.510
<i>No enemies to be seen.</i>

12:58.010 --> 13:00.600
<i>I've returned to when I was newly born.</i>

13:01.790 --> 13:05.510
<i>Is this the end? No...</i>

13:06.510 --> 13:07.980
These are...

13:11.170 --> 13:14.160
memories of my last life?

13:19.120 --> 13:20.060
Your Highness...

13:21.750 --> 13:23.060
<i>That voice...</i>

13:27.880 --> 13:30.480
It's been many years, Your Highness.

13:31.280 --> 13:32.600
Randall...

13:33.220 --> 13:36.910
<i>My heir, and the man who was set 
to inherit the kingdom after my death.</i>

13:36.910 --> 13:41.050
If you're really Randall, 
I'd like to know why, after I died,

13:41.050 --> 13:45.600
some people in this world started thinking 
of themselves as better than others.

13:46.850 --> 13:50.300
But you won't have an answer 
for me, will you?

13:50.700 --> 13:52.470
That is correct, Your Majesty!

13:56.240 --> 13:58.420
<i>This isn't good.</i>

14:01.530 --> 14:05.870
<i>If I keep going, I might end up 
running into the Goddess Alistia.</i>

14:06.230 --> 14:11.320
This was supposed to be a test of 
mental strength? I don't like it.

14:15.450 --> 14:19.210
I've got better things to do 
than waste my time here.

14:28.650 --> 14:30.340
There's more up there?

14:30.340 --> 14:32.140
Wh-What was that?

14:33.900 --> 14:35.230
I see!

14:35.230 --> 14:37.560
So it's connected to the spaces 
where the others are?

14:38.070 --> 14:40.850
Did you do this?

14:40.850 --> 14:44.520
Yeah. I didn't feel like 
continuing straight ahead.

14:44.910 --> 14:48.620
How could she destroy such a strange space?

14:49.640 --> 14:51.710
Just who are you?

14:56.720 --> 14:58.560
Just a simple squire,

14:59.280 --> 15:01.180
in Rafinha Bilford's service.

15:02.220 --> 15:08.280
If you're her squire, tell her not 
to hate her classmate so much.

15:09.560 --> 15:12.890
I'm not here to be her enemy.

15:13.650 --> 15:16.730
I don't think she hates you.

15:16.730 --> 15:17.830
She does!

15:17.830 --> 15:22.900
She tries to stay away from me as best 
she can and won't look me in the eye!

15:23.630 --> 15:28.360
Then maybe she's upset 
with the way you treat Leone.

15:28.810 --> 15:32.710
I'm the daughter of this 
kingdom's chancellor.

15:32.710 --> 15:35.170
I need to be careful.

15:36.130 --> 15:38.380
Though, to be honest...

15:38.380 --> 15:39.620
Oh?

15:41.470 --> 15:45.460
I do feel I went a little too far.

15:45.800 --> 15:48.580
Okay. I'll tell her for you.

15:49.050 --> 15:51.260
So, you think we can get out of here?

15:52.140 --> 15:55.740
I'm sick of this place. It just 
brings back all my bad memories.

15:55.740 --> 15:57.400
Me too.

15:57.400 --> 16:00.750
So I figured I'd bust my way out.

16:00.750 --> 16:01.730
Want to join me?

16:02.200 --> 16:04.140
That sounds fun.

16:04.140 --> 16:05.880
Let's go together.

16:05.880 --> 16:07.600
Okay, let's go.

16:07.600 --> 16:08.680
Wait.

16:17.110 --> 16:20.570
Is that your Gift?

16:20.570 --> 16:23.540
Yes. I'll take you to the top.

16:25.500 --> 16:27.350
Wow!

16:27.350 --> 16:28.720
You don't even need a Flying Gear!

16:28.970 --> 16:31.480
Stop! What are you doing to my brother?

16:31.480 --> 16:34.560
Move! You're wrong about this!

16:36.160 --> 16:38.570
That's... Leon?

16:39.270 --> 16:42.320
My brother's a holy knight now!

16:42.320 --> 16:44.590
He's an inspiration to everyone!

16:44.590 --> 16:46.550
Why are you being so mean?

16:47.010 --> 16:48.920
It's all a lie!

16:48.920 --> 16:50.520
You'll understand some day!

16:51.170 --> 16:55.630
Curse you! And on the very day 
my son became a holy knight!

16:55.630 --> 16:57.490
What are you going to do to Leon?

16:57.490 --> 17:00.460
Mother... Father...

17:00.830 --> 17:04.460
<i>Those wounds... She's already 
expended a great deal of her mana.</i>

17:05.330 --> 17:09.160
<i>She must have overcome many 
fierce battles to reach this point.</i>

17:10.000 --> 17:14.580
I'll... I'll defeat you 
and keep going forward!

17:14.960 --> 17:17.380
I'll defeat my brother Leon!

17:18.640 --> 17:21.570
Go on ahead. I'll help her.

17:23.010 --> 17:27.090
I won't let you take another step forward, 
if you're going to hurt my child!

17:27.090 --> 17:29.510
Begone! Go!

17:29.930 --> 17:32.730
I'll protect Leon, 
even at the cost of my life!

17:37.070 --> 17:39.570
Begone, traitor!

17:40.650 --> 17:42.330
Sorry to interrupt!

17:45.260 --> 17:47.070
I-Inglis?

17:47.070 --> 17:48.660
I'm glad I made it.

17:50.870 --> 17:52.500
How did you get here?

17:53.490 --> 17:54.960
I broke through the walls.

17:55.320 --> 17:57.140
That's crazy...

17:57.140 --> 17:59.580
That's not how the test is supposed to work.

17:59.580 --> 18:01.440
Nobody said I couldn't!

18:02.000 --> 18:04.250
I won't let you hurt my brother!

18:04.250 --> 18:06.400
I'll protect Leon, no matter what!

18:08.870 --> 18:10.310
Inglis?

18:10.310 --> 18:11.620
I'll handle them.

18:17.990 --> 18:19.740
Y-You're...

18:20.080 --> 18:23.020
It's hard for you or your friends 
to fight them, right?

18:23.020 --> 18:25.590
It's easier for me.

18:25.590 --> 18:27.700
Yeah, thanks.

18:29.260 --> 18:31.510
Th-Thank you.

18:31.510 --> 18:35.880
I'd like to apologize for 
hurting you the other day.

18:36.550 --> 18:37.660
I'm sorry.

18:38.310 --> 18:39.900
No, it's not...

18:40.130 --> 18:43.020
Liselotte's actually a nice girl, huh?

18:43.020 --> 18:45.840
That "actually" was unnecessary!

18:49.020 --> 18:52.420
Now, let's head for the top floor.

18:54.870 --> 18:56.730
Hurry up!

19:01.980 --> 19:03.530
Wow!

19:04.400 --> 19:06.700
She doesn't even need a Flying Gear, right?

19:06.700 --> 19:08.830
You just said that!

19:10.300 --> 19:11.780
Welcome back.

19:12.800 --> 19:14.480
I guess we made it out.

19:14.940 --> 19:15.750
Yeah.

19:16.140 --> 19:17.670
Huh?

19:17.670 --> 19:21.390
You came out of a different door 
than the one you went in!

19:21.390 --> 19:24.370
And the three of you all 
came out of the same door?

19:24.370 --> 19:27.760
Nothing really unusual happened.

19:27.760 --> 19:29.720
Really?

19:30.590 --> 19:32.620
That's a huge lie.

19:32.270 --> 19:35.270
Maybe it's broken...

19:32.620 --> 19:35.280
You two helped me on the way, too...

19:35.810 --> 19:38.090
You don't want to do it 
all over again, right?

19:39.380 --> 19:43.400
Principal Miliera, 
this means we passed, right?

19:44.640 --> 19:47.050
Well, you did come out of the door.

19:47.050 --> 19:49.660
So I guess I have to pass you.

19:50.220 --> 19:53.140
You pass. Congratulations!

19:55.160 --> 19:56.600
Where are Rani and Pram?

19:57.060 --> 19:58.920
Oh, did she pass already?

19:58.920 --> 20:02.240
No, she failed almost immediately.

20:02.240 --> 20:04.810
A hole opened, and she got tossed out.

20:05.270 --> 20:08.520
I was supposed to win this!

20:08.780 --> 20:11.360
I told you to give it up.

20:12.270 --> 20:13.360
Rani!

20:13.360 --> 20:14.360
Chris!

20:14.790 --> 20:16.950
I finally made it out!

20:17.860 --> 20:20.400
Rafinha, you pass!

20:20.710 --> 20:22.570
Welcome back, Rani!

20:22.570 --> 20:23.680
Congratulations!

20:23.680 --> 20:24.900
Thank you!

20:24.900 --> 20:27.150
You two both passed, right?

20:27.150 --> 20:28.930
Huh? Oh, of course.

20:28.930 --> 20:30.400
I guess...

20:30.400 --> 20:32.080
You guess?

20:32.080 --> 20:33.210
Never mind.

20:33.210 --> 20:34.900
Anyway, were you okay?

20:34.900 --> 20:37.040
I'm so tired!

20:37.040 --> 20:39.890
I'm gonna eat a lot and then sleep!

20:40.350 --> 20:43.350
When you're tired, you move 
around in your sleep a lot.

20:43.350 --> 20:45.430
It's going to be a rough night.

20:45.430 --> 20:47.690
That's so mean, Chris!

20:47.690 --> 20:50.170
S-Sorry, it's my fault...

20:50.520 --> 20:53.930
No! No! That's not what I meant!

20:53.930 --> 20:55.430
If that's what this is about...

21:00.040 --> 21:01.690
You gonna be okay, Leone?

21:01.690 --> 21:03.780
I-I'm fine.

21:03.780 --> 21:05.190
It'll be fine.

21:05.190 --> 21:07.750
Liselotte's actually a good girl.

21:07.750 --> 21:09.240
Yeah, I know.

21:10.870 --> 21:14.460
Why are you standing outside 
my room and talking about me?

21:16.550 --> 21:18.930
Welcome to <i>our</i> room!

21:18.930 --> 21:21.660
Th-Thanks for having me.

21:22.120 --> 21:24.250
Now, come inside.

21:28.180 --> 21:29.600
Hey...

21:31.720 --> 21:33.550
I was just kidding.

21:33.780 --> 21:36.760
Liselotte can be surprisingly silly.

21:37.030 --> 21:40.240
I'd prefer you said I had a sense of humor.

21:40.530 --> 21:43.040
Wow, this room is so cute!

21:43.040 --> 21:45.870
This isn't the furniture 
that came with the room!

21:45.870 --> 21:48.440
I brought in the same kind I have at home!

21:48.810 --> 21:53.020
Hey, I brought a lot of party things 
so we could have a celebration!

21:53.020 --> 21:54.670
A celebration of what?

21:54.670 --> 21:59.520
You know... making up... and stuff.

21:59.520 --> 22:02.100
I brought lots of food, too!

22:02.100 --> 22:05.830
You've still got room for food 
after all you ate at dinner?!

23:45.070 --> 23:50.060
